{
 "plan": {
  "title": "Household Survey Coverage",
  "subtitle": "Overview of survey submissions by village, enumerator, and time trends",
  "panels": [
   {
    "id": "p1",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Total Submissions",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM \"household_survey\"",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p2",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Unique Villages",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT \"village\") AS n FROM \"household_survey\"",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p3",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Unique Enumerators",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT \"enumerator_name\") AS n FROM \"household_survey\"",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p4",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Submissions by Village",
    "sql": "SELECT \"village\", COUNT(*) AS count FROM \"household_survey\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 15",
    "x": "village",
    "y": [
     "count"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p5",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Submissions by Enumerator",
    "sql": "SELECT \"enumerator_name\", COUNT(*) AS count FROM \"household_survey\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10",
    "x": "enumerator_name",
    "y": [
     "count"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p6",
    "kind": "line",
    "title": "Monthly Submission Trend",
    "sql": "SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', CAST(\"start\" AS TIMESTAMP)) AS month, COUNT(*) AS total FROM \"household_survey\" WHERE \"start\" IS NOT NULL AND \"start\" != '' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1",
    "x": "month",
    "y": [
     "total"
    ]
   }
  ],
  "narrative": "The dashboard tracks the progress of the household survey across {{p1}} total submissions. Data collection spans {{p2}} distinct villages and involves {{p3}} unique enumerators. The bar chart for village coverage shows that the highest activity is concentrated in the top locations, with the leading village accounting for a significant portion of the {{p4}} data points. Similarly, enumerator performance varies, with the most active enumerator responsible for {{p5}} records. Over time, the submission trend visualized in the line chart indicates fluctuations in fieldwork intensity, peaking at {{p6}} submissions in the busiest month."
 },
